--- STEP 0. Working baseline
    checkout -> HTTP 200
    current upstream in ConfigMap:
              proxy_pass http://checkout-svc/checkout;

--- STEP 1. Inject the migration bug: use the Compose name instead of the Service name
    injection verified in the cluster:
              proxy_pass http://checkout-fn/checkout;
    rollout status after restart (bounded):
      Waiting for deployment "gateway" rollout to finish: 1 out of 2 new replicas have been updated...

--- STEP 2. Symptom as a user sees it
    checkout x5 -> 200 200 200 200 200 
    NOTE: the lab predicts 503 here. This platform returns 200 because the broken config
    cannot pass the readiness gate, so the old gateway pods keep serving. The failure is
    therefore visible to operators (CrashLoopBackOff) but not to users. That is the
    intended behaviour of running two replicas behind a rolling update.

--- STEP 3. Diagnose (lab 4.3 workflow: pods -> service -> endpoints -> logs)
    3a. are the gateway pods running?
        gateway-6dbd8ff985-2v8n5   0/1   CrashLoopBackOff   3 (30s ago)   67s
        gateway-84c49f68df-brvd5   1/1   Running            0             103s
        gateway-84c49f68df-skkrv   1/1   Running            0             109s
    3b. does a Service named 'checkout-fn' exist?
        NO SUCH SERVICE -> DNS for checkout-fn cannot resolve
    3c. what Services actually exist?
        checkout-svc  10.43.179.188  80/TCP
        gateway-svc  10.43.214.131  80/TCP
        inventory-svc  10.43.30.95  80/TCP
        postgres-svc  10.43.69.254  5432/TCP
        pricing-svc  10.43.69.60  80/TCP
    3d. endpoints behind the real Service (backend itself is healthy):
        checkout-svc-zc9js   IPv4   3003   10.42.0.69,10.42.0.73   168m
    3e. the gateway's own words:
        2026/08/14 15:32:48 [emerg] 1#1: host not found in upstream "checkout-fn" in /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf:17
        nginx: [emerg] host not found in upstream "checkout-fn" in /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf:17
        (previous) 2026/08/14 15:32:48 [emerg] 1#1: host not found in upstream "checkout-fn" in /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf:17
        (previous) nginx: [emerg] host not found in upstream "checkout-fn" in /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf:17

    ROOT CAUSE: the gateway resolves the container name from Compose, but in Kubernetes
    the stable name is the Service. The backend was never unhealthy.

--- STEP 4. Fix and prove
    deployment "gateway" successfully rolled out
    restored upstream:
              proxy_pass http://checkout-svc/checkout;
    checkout x5 -> 200 200 200 200 200 
